<main id="content" tabindex="-1">

<div class="page-head"><div><h1>Add worker</h1><p>A worker is a machine that hosts terminal sessions. Choose how it joins your space.</p></div></div>
<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="join-one-step" data-join-panel>
  <h2 id="join-one-step">Add a Worker in one step</h2>
  <p class="muted">Creates a one-time invitation key and shows one command with everything the new machine needs: this Hub's address, its full fingerprint and the key. Run it on the machine that should become a Worker.</p>
  <form method="post" hx-post="/workers/add/join" hx-target="#join-result" hx-swap="innerHTML" hx-disabled-elt="find button[type=submit]">
    <div class="field">
      <label for="join-name">Name (optional)</label>
      <input type="text" id="join-name" name="name" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" maxlength="64" aria-describedby="join-name-help">
      <span id="join-name-help" class="muted">The Worker's name and the name of the key in the list. Without a name, the Worker announces its host name.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="join-ttl">Valid for (at most 1 week)</label>
      <select id="join-ttl" name="ttl">
        <option value="1h" selected>1 hour</option>
        <option value="4h">4 hours</option>
        <option value="8h">8 hours</option>
        <option value="24h">24 hours</option>
        <option value="1w">1 week</option>
        
      </select>
    </div>
    <button type="submit">Create the join command</button>
    <div id="join-result" aria-live="polite"></div>
  </form>
  <noscript><p class="muted">Creating a join command needs JavaScript in this browser.</p></noscript>
  
  <script src="/onboarding.js" defer></script>
</section>
<div class="method-grid">
<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="pair-form">
  <h2 id="pair-form">Pair with a code</h2>
  <p class="muted">Start pairing on the machine that should become a Worker (for example with <code>minion worker pair</code>). It shows a code like <code>MN-ABCD-EFGH</code>. Enter that code here.</p>
  <form method="post" hx-post="/workers/add" hx-target="#pair-result" hx-swap="innerHTML" hx-disabled-elt="find button[type=submit]">
    <div class="field">
      <label for="pair-code">Pairing code</label>
      <input type="text" id="pair-code" name="code" placeholder="MN-ABCD-EFGH" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="characters" spellcheck="false" required maxlength="32" aria-describedby="pair-code-help">
      <span id="pair-code-help" class="muted">Capital or small letters, with or without hyphens.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="pair-name">Name (optional)</label>
      <input type="text" id="pair-name" name="name" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" maxlength="64" aria-describedby="pair-name-help">
      <span id="pair-name-help" class="muted">Without a name, the Worker keeps the name it announces.</span>
    </div>
    <button type="submit">Add the Worker</button>
    <div id="pair-result" aria-live="polite"></div>
  </form>
  <noscript><p class="muted">Adding a Worker needs JavaScript in this browser.</p></noscript>
</section>
<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="invite-method">
  <h2 id="invite-method">Use an invitation</h2>
  <p class="muted">For a reusable key (many machines, for example from a script or an image) or an admin's infrastructure key. The key is shown once when you create it, together with commands that start the Worker and pin this Hub's fingerprint.</p>
  <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/invitations">Create an invitation key</a>
</section>
</div>

    </main>